1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:09,716
In 2025, the world burned 167 billion cubic meters of gas through flaring: an estimated 54
billion dollars in wasted value.

2
00:00:09,716 --> 00:00:12,391
This is also a community issue.

3
00:00:12,391 --> 00:00:19,973
A study in Eagle Ford associated high nearby flaring with fifty percent higher odds of preterm
birth.

4
00:00:19,973 --> 00:00:26,217
Operators face a practical question: with limited capital, which flares should they fix first?

5
00:00:26,217 --> 00:00:30,230
FlareWise connects that investment decision to the people downwind.

6
00:00:30,230 --> 00:00:39,150
Recovering gas creates a financial reason to act; targeting the right sources makes community
priorities part of the investment case.

7
00:00:40,350 --> 00:00:47,650
Our users are operator capital teams, working with health, safety and environment teams and
public-health planners.

8
00:00:47,650 --> 00:00:55,406
In South Texas, we evaluate 392 candidates using gas volumes, economics, hourly winds and real
Census demographics.

9
00:00:55,406 --> 00:00:57,688
Give us ten million dollars.

10
00:00:57,688 --> 00:01:06,812
Financial delivers 33.6 million in projected seven-year net present value and a 5.2 percent
reduction in our population-weighted exposure index.

11
00:01:06,812 --> 00:01:15,938
Now switch to Balanced: retain 95.5 percent of financial value while more than doubling that
index improvement to 10.6 percent.

12
00:01:15,938 --> 00:01:18,219
Community prioritization reaches 22.2 percent.

13
00:01:18,219 --> 00:01:24,150
The creative step is making these competing priorities one explicit, inspectable investment
decision.

14
00:01:25,350 --> 00:01:29,417
Underneath, integer optimization selects actual projects within budget.

15
00:01:29,417 --> 00:01:36,533
Annual analysis uses every hour of weather, while Census attribution shows which tracts
benefit.

16
00:01:36,533 --> 00:01:40,092
This interactive three-dimensional replay follows moving emissions.

17
00:01:40,092 --> 00:01:47,717
Compare capture installed at ten p.m.: new emissions shrink while previously emitted material
continues downwind.

18
00:01:47,717 --> 00:01:53,817
GPU-instanced rendering delivered about sixty frames per second in our local test.

19
00:01:53,817 --> 00:01:58,900
We also trained a twelve-band Sentinel-2 U-Net for industrial-smoke segmentation.

20
00:01:58,900 --> 00:02:07,542
On 374 held-out images, its intersection-over-union reached 47.1 percent, versus 23.6 percent
for a simple RGB heuristic.

21
00:02:07,542 --> 00:02:11,608
These are saved predictions and a reproducible model.

22
00:02:11,608 --> 00:02:14,150
Forty-one tests verify the build.

23
00:02:15,350 --> 00:02:18,870
TotalEnergies has committed to ending routine flaring by 2030.

24
00:02:18,870 --> 00:02:23,171
FlareWise could help turn that commitment into a prioritized project pipeline.

25
00:02:23,171 --> 00:02:29,820
Our proposed first pilot pairs one asset team's engineering costs and infrastructure
constraints with local environmental validation.

26
00:02:29,820 --> 00:02:35,686
Success means a shortlist ready for engineering review, with economics and community priorities
assessed together.

27
00:02:35,686 --> 00:02:40,379
We would measure recovered gas, project returns and independently verified emissions changes.

28
00:02:40,379 --> 00:02:45,071
Then expand basin by basin through regional weather, population and infrastructure data.

29
00:02:45,071 --> 00:02:48,591
Our global inventory already provides discovery across 77 countries.

30
00:02:48,591 --> 00:02:57,195
Our vision is a new standard for climate investment: every dollar evaluated for both economic
return and the communities it can benefit.

31
00:02:57,195 --> 00:02:59,150
FlareWise makes that future actionable.
